    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d794">

                <pb facs="0806" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51/1654</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State (Welles) to
                        the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs (Alling)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-07-23">July 23, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I suggest that you discuss this problem<anchor n="69" xml:id="d794-f1"/> with Dr.
                        Berle,<anchor n="70" xml:id="d794-f2"/> and I further suggest that, unless
                    you see some objection, the Bureau of the Budget be requested to give its advice
                    as to the best way of handling this situation. It is my understanding that the
                    President has decided that some arrangement must be made whereby the Greek
                    Government can be kept going.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d794-f3"/> The amounts
                    involved are relatively small and <pb facs="0807" n="801" xml:id="pg801"/> it
                    would seem to me that the time has come for us to consider the desirability of
                    ascertaining whether the Congress would approve a government-to-government
                    credit for arrangements of this character with the refugee governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d794-f1" n="69" xml:id="d794-f1-content">
                <p>See memorandum of conversation, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d794-f2" n="70" xml:id="d794-f2-content">
                <p>Adolf A. Berle, Jr., Assistant Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d794-f3" n="71" xml:id="d794-f3-content">
                <p>In a letter of December 14, 1942, to the Secretary of the Treasury (Morgenthau),
                    the Secretary of State said: “King George of Greece and the Greek Premier,
                    during their visit to this country last June, stated that the financial
                    situation of the Greek Government was rapidly deteriorating and appealed to this
                    Government for financial assistance. It is my understanding that the President
                    has decided that some arrangement must be made by which the Greek Government can
                    be kept going.” (868.51/1662) Regarding the visit of King George II to the
                    United States, see bracketed note, <ref target="#pg797">p. 797</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
